    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "\n<div class=\"august-issue-banner\">\n    <div class=\"august-banner-badge\">🔔 14 Official Languages Edition</div>\n    <div class=\"august-banner-content\">\n        <h4>Vol. 2026 — Master Editorial Hub (Part 1)</h4>\n        <p>Welcome to the central editorial hub for beginner language learners (CEFR A0–A1). Frequency research demonstrates that these 10 core verbs account for up to 80% of daily spoken output across all 14 of our official languages!</p>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n<section style=\"margin: 2rem 0; padding: 1.5rem; background: #faf7f2; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid var(--ink-light, #e2e8f0);\">\n    <h3 style=\"margin-top:0; color:var(--post-palette-accent, #d97706);\">🌐 14 Official Languages Navigation Hub</h3>\n    <p style=\"color:var(--ink-secondary); margin-bottom:1.25rem;\">Select any target language below to explore its deep-dive A0–A1 guide, including conjugation highlights, collocations, false-friend traps, and high-frequency idioms:</p>\n    \n    <div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 0.75rem;\">\n        <a href=\"top-10-verbs-en.html\" style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; background: #ffffff; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-decoration: none; color: #1e293b; font-weight: 600;\">🇬🇧 English Guide ↗</a>\n        <a href=\"top-10-verbs-fr.html\" style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; background: #ffffff; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-decoration: none; color: #1e293b; font-weight: 600;\">🇫🇷 French Guide ↗</a>\n        <a href=\"top-10-verbs-it.html\" style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; background: #ffffff; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-decoration: none; color: #1e293b; font-weight: 600;\">🇮🇹 Italian Guide ↗</a>\n        <a href=\"top-10-verbs-ru.html\" style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; background: #ffffff; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-decoration: none; color: #1e293b; font-weight: 600;\">🇷🇺 Russian Guide ↗</a>\n        <a href=\"top-10-verbs-el.html\" style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; background: #ffffff; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-decoration: none; color: #1e293b; font-weight: 600;\">🇬🇷 Greek Guide ↗</a>\n        <a href=\"top-10-verbs-tt.html\" style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; background: #ffffff; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-decoration: none; color: #1e293b; font-weight: 600;\">🌐 Tatar Guide ↗</a>\n        <a href=\"top-10-verbs-ba.html\" style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; background: #ffffff; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-decoration: none; color: #1e293b; font-weight: 600;\">🌐 Bashkir Guide ↗</a>\n        <a href=\"top-10-verbs-br.html\" style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; background: #ffffff; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-decoration: none; color: #1e293b; font-weight: 600;\">🌐 Breton Guide ↗</a>\n        <a href=\"top-10-verbs-pt.html\" style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; background: #ffffff; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-decoration: none; color: #1e293b; font-weight: 600;\">🇵🇹 Portuguese Guide ↗</a>\n        <a href=\"top-10-verbs-es.html\" style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; background: #ffffff; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-decoration: none; color: #1e293b; font-weight: 600;\">🇪🇸 Spanish Guide ↗</a>\n        <a href=\"top-10-verbs-de.html\" style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; background: #ffffff; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-decoration: none; color: #1e293b; font-weight: 600;\">🇩🇪 German Guide ↗</a>\n        <a href=\"top-10-verbs-hy.html\" style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; background: #ffffff; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-decoration: none; color: #1e293b; font-weight: 600;\">🇦🇲 Armenian Guide ↗</a>\n        <a href=\"top-10-verbs-ka.html\" style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; background: #ffffff; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-decoration: none; color: #1e293b; font-weight: 600;\">🇬🇪 Georgian Guide ↗</a>\n        <a href=\"top-10-verbs-cv.html\" style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; background: #ffffff; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; text-decoration: none; color: #1e293b; font-weight: 600;\">🌐 Chuvash Guide ↗</a>\n    </div>\n</section>\n\n<div class=\"verb-map-container\">\n    <h3 class=\"verb-map-title\">🗺️ The 10 Essential Core Verbs (Part 1 Focus)</h3>\n    <p style=\"margin-bottom:1rem; color:var(--ink-secondary);\">These 10 essential action anchors power everyday speech across all 14 official languages:</p>\n\n    <div class=\"verb-map-grid\">\n        <div class=\"verb-node-card\"><strong>1. To Be</strong> — Existence, identity, states, age.</div>\n        <div class=\"verb-node-card\"><strong>2. To Have</strong> — Possession, physical states, obligations.</div>\n        <div class=\"verb-node-card\"><strong>3. To Think</strong> — Expressing opinions, beliefs, thoughts.</div>\n        <div class=\"verb-node-card\"><strong>4. To Know</strong> — Facts, skills, familiarity.</div>\n        <div class=\"verb-node-card\"><strong>5. To Like</strong> — Preferences, tastes, enjoyment.</div>\n        <div class=\"verb-node-card\"><strong>6. To Want / Would like</strong> — Desires, orders, polite requests.</div>\n        <div class=\"verb-node-card\"><strong>7. To Go / Be going to</strong> — Movement, travel, future intention.</div>\n        <div class=\"verb-node-card\"><strong>8. To Can</strong> — Modal ability, possibility, permission.</div>\n        <div class=\"verb-node-card\"><strong>9. To Eat</strong> — Meals, food consumption, dining out.</div>\n        <div class=\"verb-node-card\"><strong>10. To Drink</strong> — Beverages, hydration, social drinks.</div>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"printable-reference-card\">\n    <div class=\"printable-reference-header\">\n        <h3 class=\"printable-reference-title\">📋 COSYmagazine Top 10 Core Verbs Printable Reference Sheet</h3>\n        <button type=\"button\" class=\"print-download-btn\" onclick=\"window.print()\">🖨️ Print / Download Table</button>\n    </div>\n    <table class=\"printable-reference-table\">\n        <thead>\n            <tr>\n                <th>#</th>\n                <th>Verb Anchor</th>\n                <th>Core Meaning & Function</th>\n                <th>Key Example Sentence</th>\n            </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n            <tr><td>1</td><td><strong>To Be</strong></td><td>Existence, identity, states, age, location</td><td>I am ready. / She is a doctor.</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>2</td><td><strong>To Have</strong></td><td>Possession, relationships, physical states</td><td>I have a phone. / She has brown eyes.</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>3</td><td><strong>To Think</strong></td><td>Opinions, thoughts, beliefs</td><td>I think it is a great idea.</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>4</td><td><strong>To Know</strong></td><td>Facts, familiarity, skills (know how to)</td><td>I know the answer. / She knows how to swim.</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>5</td><td><strong>To Like</strong></td><td>Preferences, tastes, enjoyment</td><td>I like learning languages.</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>6</td><td><strong>To Want / Would Like</strong></td><td>Desires, ordering, polite requests</td><td>I want to learn English. / I'd like a coffee.</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>7</td><td><strong>To Go / Be Going To</strong></td><td>Movement, travel, future intention</td><td>I go to work by train. / I'm going to travel.</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>8</td><td><strong>To Can</strong></td><td>Modal ability, requests, permission</td><td>I can speak English. / Can you help me?</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>9</td><td><strong>To Eat</strong></td><td>Meals, food consumption, dining out</td><td>I eat fresh fruit every morning.</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>10</td><td><strong>To Drink</strong></td><td>Beverages, hydration, social drinks</td><td>I drink two litres of water daily.</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n    </table>\n</div>"
    },
